      "content": "Certainly, here are more detailed explanations of those arguments:\n\n1. **Pseudoscientific Racial Superiority**:\n   - **IQ Testing**: Advocacy for segregation included claims based on IQ tests, which were said to prove racial differences in intelligence. Supporters of segregation often presented biased or misinterpreted test results to suggest that Black individuals were intellectually inferior to Whites.\n   - **Biological Determinism**: Segregationists often cited the belief that biological factors determined intelligence and behavior. They argued that racial differences were innate and immutable, determined by one's biological heritage. This was often reinforced through unscientific interpretations of physical differences.\n\n2. **Social Darwinism**:\n   - **Survival of the Fittest**: Segregation proponents argued that the principle of survival of the fittest applied to human races. They believed that segregation allowed the superior \"White race\" to thrive by keeping them in a watershed of their own culture, while the supposedly inferior races were kept in subservient, less desirable roles.\n   - **Social Roles and Hierarchies**: It was argued that societies maintain social order when races remained in their natural hierarchies. Black people were often characterized as possessing inherent traits that made them",
